  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessment poultry curriculum Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is aimed at strengthening the bilateral engagement of the Embassy of the Netherlands in Dar es Salaam, Tanzania, and the Tanzanian Ministry of Livestock and Fisheries. The underlying Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), which was recently extended for another five years (2024 &#x2013; 2029), is proof of a longstanding collaboration of the two countries.The purpose of this project is to improve poultry education at the Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) level in Tanzania. After the project, based on the output of contractor, the knowledge institute the Livestock Training Agency (LITA) knows -	which steps to take to set up a modern poultry curriculum, -	how to make use of existing curricula and -	which steps to take for accreditation. Additionally the contractor of the project will come up with knowledge sharing and capacity building follow-up to make sure the curriculum can be developed at LITA.The project sets out to contribute to a resilient and future-proof poultry sector by improving the curriculum offer and support and encourage students to increase their understanding of the poultry industry.</narrative>
  </description>
